PROJECT:
Th3 Thirty3 is an autonomous AI cybersecurity agent integrating multi-LLM support, OSINT tools, and anonymity networks for ethical assessments.

SUMMARY:
This project functions as a centralized command center for security professionals. It orchestrates various AI models (local and cloud) to analyze threat intelligence gathered from Shodan and OSINT sources. The system runs within a secure architecture, utilizing Docker for tool isolation and TOR/VPN services for anonymity, all managed via a Node.js backend and React frontend.

STEPS:
1. Initialize the Node.js project structure for backend services and frontend interface management.
2. Configure Docker Compose to orchestrate the Kali Linux and TOR proxy containers securely.
3. Implement the LLM service adapter to route queries between Ollama, OpenAI, and Anthropic.
4. Develop the Shodan service module to fetch vulnerability data and asset information via API.
5. Create the VPN service controller to manage network rotation and proxy configurations automatically.
6. Build the OSINT service wrapper to execute reconnaissance tools and parse their outputs.
7. Construct the Express API routes to expose service functionalities to the frontend dashboard.
8. Develop the React frontend with components for chat, metrics, and tool configuration.

